{title: 376 - All Things Are Thine}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #376 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 376}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]All things [Eb/Bb]are [Ab]Thine; [Bbm/F]nogift [Db/Ab]have [Eb/Bb]we,
[Fm]Lord [Eb/Bb]of [Bbm]all [Eb]gifts, [Ab]to of [Fm]fer [Cm/G]Thee;
[Ab]And hence with [Eb]grateful [Ab]hearts today,
[Eb/Bb]Thine [Bbm]own [Db/Ab]before [Fm/C]Thy [Bbm/Db]feetwe [Eb/Bb]lay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Thy will [Eb/Bb]was [Ab]in [Bbm/F]the [Cm/G]builder's [Eb/Bb]thought;
[Fm]Thy [Eb/Bb]hand [Bbm]unseen [Ab]amidst [Fm]us [Cm/G]wrought;
[Ab]Thro' mortal [Eb]motive, [Ab]scheme and [Bbm/Db]plan,
[Eb/Bb]Thy [Bbm]wise, [Db/Ab]eternal [Fm/C]purpose [Eb/Bb]ran.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]No lack [Eb/Bb]Thy [Ab]perfect [Cm/G]fullness [Eb/Bb]knew;
[Fm]For [Eb/Bb]human needs [Ab]and longings [Cm/G]grew
[Ab]This house of [Eb]prayer- [Ab]this home of [Bbm/Db]rest.
[Eb/Bb]Here [Bbm]may [Db/Ab]Thy [Ab]saints [Bbm/Db]be [Fm/C]often [Eb/Bb]blessed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]In weakness and [Bbm/F]in [Cm/G]want [Db/Ab]we [Eb/Bb]call
[Fm]On [Eb/Bb]Thee, [Bbm]for [Eb]whom [Ab]the heav'ns [Fm]are [Cm/G]small;
[Ab]Thy glory [Eb]is [Ab]Thy children's [Bbm/Db]good,
[Eb/Bb]Thy [Bbm]joy [Db/Ab]Thy [Ab]tender [Fm/C]Fatherhood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Ab]O Father! deign [Bbm/F]these [Cm/G]walls [Db/Ab]to [Eb/Bb]bless;
[Fm]Make [Eb/Bb]this [Bbm]the abode [Ab]of [Cm/G]righteousness,
[Ab]And let these [Eb]doors [G7]a [Ab]gateway [Bbm/Db]be
[Eb/Bb]To [Bbm]lead [Db/Ab]us [Ab]from [Bbm/Db]ourselves [Eb/Bb]to [Ab]Thee!
{end_of_verse}
